From: j7
Subject: j7: drop the compiled-in picture from the desktop

The photograph painted, but every dark part of it was a hole: the desktop is painted on
top of it, and the tile seen on the phone had black blocks wherever the picture was
dark.  Stop shipping the picture inside the kernel - one half-size RGB565 photograph is
not a wallpaper anyway - and paint nothing where the client painted nothing, so the
desktop keeps one flat, graded background.

A raw picture is still read from /var/mobile/j7wall.raw (or j7wall=<path>) when that
file exists, and that path now opens the file before allocating the buffer and frees
the buffer when the read fails, instead of leaving four megabytes behind and painting
half of it.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -80,9 +80,6 @@
 #include <sys/kauth.h>
 #include <sys/vfs_context.h>
 #endif
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE)
-#include "j7wall_data.h"    /* tools/j7wall.py output: the picture below, RGB565 */
-#endif
 
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_HEROLTE)
